---
title: Osso Buco
servings: 6
prepTime: 15 min
cookTime: 2 hr
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 8/10
source: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/giada-de-laurentiis/osso-buco-recipe-2013380
tags: Alcohol, Beef
---

Place the @rosemary{1%sprig}(fresh), @thyme{1%sprig}(fresh), @bay leaf{1}, and @whole cloves{2}
into #cheesecloth and secure with #kitchen twine{}. This will be your bouquet garni.

For the @veal shanks{3}(whole, about 1# each, trimmed), pat dry with paper towels to remove any excess moisture.
Veal shanks will brown better when they are dry.
Secure the meat to the bone with #kitchen twine{}.
Season each shank with @salt and @ground pepper{}.
Dredge the shanks in @flour{1%cup}, shaking off excess.

In a large #Dutch oven{} pot, heat @vegetable oil{1/2%cup} until smoking.
Add tied veal shanks to the hot pan and brown all sides, about 3 minutes per side.
Remove browned shanks and reserve.

Dice the @onion{1}(small), @carrot{1}, and @celery{1%stalk} into 1/2" cubes.
Add the vegetables into the same pot.
Season with @salt at this point to help draw out the moisture from the vegetables.

Saute until soft and translucent, about ~{8%minutes}.
Add the @tomato paste{1%tbsp} and mix well.
Return browned shanks to the pan and add the @dry white wine{1%cup} and reduce liquid by half, about ~{5%minutes}.
Add the bouquet garni (herb mix) and @chicken stock{2%cups} and bring to a boil.

Reduce heat to low, cover pan and simmer for about ~{90%min} or until the meat is falling off the bone.
Check every 15 minutes, turning shanks and adding more @?chicken stock{1%cup} as necessary.
The level of cooking liquid should always be about 3/4 the way up the shank.

= Serving =
Carefully remove the cooked shanks from the pot and place in decorative serving platter.
Cut off the kitchen twine and discard.

Remove and discard bouquet garni from the pot.

Pour all the juices and sauce from the pot over the shanks.
Garnish with @parsley{3%tbsp}(chopped) and @lemon zest{1%tbsp}(grated).

